hadiths[115]{hadithnumber,text}:
"965","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Nothing afflicts the believer"
"966","Ahmad ibn Mani‘ and Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Wasiti—both narrating with the same meaning—reported to us: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Rufay‘, who said: I said to Anas ibn Malik, “Tell me something you directly heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Where did he pray the Zuhr prayer on the Day of Tarwiyah?” He replied, “In Mina.” I then asked, “Where did he pray the ‘Asr prayer on the Day of Nafir?” He answered, “In al-Abtah.” Then he added, “Do as your leaders do.” Abu ‘Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith, considered gharib (uncommon) from the narration of Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq from al-Thawri."
"967","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The believer is not afflicted by the prick of a thorn or what is worse (or greater) than that, except that by it Allah raises him in rank and removes sin from him."""
"968","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Nothing afflicts the believer, whether fatigue, grief, disease - even a worry that concerns him - except that by it, Allah removes something from his bad deeds."""
"969","Thuwair [and he is Ibn Abi Fakhitah] narrated that :His father said: ""Ali took me by the hand and said: 'Come with us to pay a visit to Al-Hasan.' So we found that Abu Musa was with him.' Ali - peace be upon him - said: 'O Abu Musa! Did you come to visit (the sick) or merely (stop by to) visit?' He said: 'No"
"970","Harithah bin Mudarrib said:""I entered upon Khabab and he had been cauterized on his stomach. He said: 'I do not know any of the Companions of the Prophet who met with the trial I have met with. Indeed I could not find a Dirham during the time of the Prophet"
"971","His father said: ""Ali took me by the hand and said: 'Come with us to pay a visit to Al-Hasan.' So we found that Abu Musa was with him.' Ali - peace be upon him - said: 'O Abu Musa! Did you come to visit (the sick) or merely (stop by to) visit?' He said: 'No, to visit (the sick).' So Ali said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""No Muslim visits (the sick) Muslims in the morning, except that sevety-thousand angels, sent Salat upon him until the evening, and he does not visit at night except that seventy thousand angels sent Salat upon him until the morning, and there will be a garden for him in Paradise."""
"972","""I entered upon Khabab and he had been cauterized on his stomach. He said: 'I do not know any of the Companions of the Prophet who met with the trial I have met with. Indeed I could not find a Dirham during the time of the Prophet, and (now) outside my house there are forty thousand. If it were not that the Messenger of Allah forbade us' - or: 'forbade' - 'from wishing for death, then I would wish for it.'"""
"973","Abdul-Aziz bin Suhaib said:""Thabit Al-Bunani and I entered upon Anas bin Malik"
"974","Jibril came to the Prophet and said: ""O Muhammad! Are you suffering?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""In the Name of Allah, I recite a prayer (Ruqyah) over you, from the evil of every person and evil eye. In the Name of Allah I recite a prayer (Ruqyah) over you, may Allah cure you."""
"975","""Thabit Al-Bunani and I entered upon Anas bin Malik, and Thabit said: 'O Abu Hamzah! I am suffering from an illness. So Anas said: 'Shall I not recite the Ruqyah of the Messenger of Allah over you?' He said: 'Why, yes.' He said: 'O Allah! Lord of mankind, removed the harm, and cure (him). Indeed You are the One Who cures, there is none who cures except you, a cure that leaves no disease.'"""
"976","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Instruct your dying to say: (La illaha illallah) 'None has the right to be worshipped but Allah"
"977","""The Messenger of Allah came to visit me while I was sick. He said: 'Do you have a will?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'For how much?' I said: 'All of my wealth, for the cause of Allah.' He said: 'What did you leave for your children?'"" He (Sa'd) said: ""They are rich in goodness.' He said: 'Will a tenth.'"" He (Sa'd) said: ""He (pbuh) continued decreasing it until he said: 'Will a third, and a third is too great.'"" (One of the narrators:) Abdur-Rahman said: ""We considered it recommended that it be less than a third, since the Messenger of Allah said: 'And a third is too great.'"""
"978","Aishah narrated:""I saw the Messenger of Allah while he was dying. He had a cup with water in it"
"979","""The Messenger of Allah said to us: 'When you attend to the sick or dying then say only good, for indeed the angels say ""Amin"" to what you say.'"" She said: ""When Abu Salamah died I went to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Abu Salamah has died.' He said: 'Then say: ""O Allah forgive me and him, and give me a good replacement for him."" She said: ""I said tat, and Allah gave a replace that was better than him: The Messenger of Allah."""
"980","""I saw the Messenger of Allah while he was dying. He had a cup with water in it, he put his hand in the cup then wiped his face with the water, then said: 'O Allah! Help me with the throes of death and the agony of death.'"""
"981","Anas bin Malik narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is nothing that the two Guardian Angels raise to Allah that they have preserved in a day or night"
"982","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him):**

Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Husām ibn al-Miṣakk narrated to us, saying: Abū Ma'shar narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm, from 'Alqamah, who said:

I heard **Abdullah** say: I heard the **Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)** say:

> *""Indeed, the soul of the believer comes out as a trickle (rashḥ), and I do not love a death like the death of a donkey.""*

It was asked: **""And what is the death of a donkey?""**

He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied:

> *""A sudden death (al-fa'ah).""*

---

**Explanation of Key Terms:**

- **"
"983","Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥalabī narrated to us, from Tammām ibn Najīḥ, from al-Ḥasan, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""There are no two guardian angels who raise to Allah what they have preserved of [the deeds of a servant] during the night or the day, and Allah finds at the beginning of the scroll and at the end of it nothing but good, except that Allah, the Most High, will say: 'Bear witness that I have forgiven My servant for what is between the two ends of the scroll.'"""
"984","Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from al-Muthannā ibn Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""The believer dies with sweat upon his forehead.""

He said: And in this chapter there is also a narration from Ibn Masʿūd. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan hadith. Some of the scholars of knowledge have said: ""We do not know of Qatādah having heard directly from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah."""
"985","The Prophet entered upon a young man while he was dying. So he said: ""How do you feel?"" He said: ""By Allah! O Messenger of Allah! Indeed I hope in Allah and I fear from my sins."" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""These two will not be gathered in a worshipper's heart at a time such as this, except that Allah will grant him what he hopes and make him safe from what he fears."""
"986","Bilal bin Yahya Al-Absiy narrated that:Hudaifah (bin Al-Yaman) said: ""When I do not announce about me to anyone"
"987","(from the Prophet) similar (to no. 984), but he did not narrate it in Marfu form, and he did not mention in it: ""An-Na'i is announcing of one's death."""
"988","Hudaifah (bin Al-Yaman) said: ""When I do not announce about me to anyone, indeed I fear that it would be An-Na'i, and I heard the Messenger of Allah prohibiting from An-Na'i."""
"989","Al-Qasim bin Muhammad narrated from Aishah:""The Prophet kissed Uthman bin Maz'un when he died"
"990","The Messenger of Alllah said: ""(Real) Patience is at the first stroke of the calamity."""
"991","""The Prophet kissed Uthman bin Maz'un when he died, and he was crying."" Or, he (one of the narrators) said: ""His eyes were brimming with tears."""
"992","Ahmad bin Mani' narrated to us, Hushaim narrated to us, Khalid, Mansur, and Hisham informed us - as for Khalid and Hisham, they said: from Muhammad and Hafsah, and Mansur said: from Muhammad, from Umm 'Atiyyah who said: ""One of the daughters of the Prophet (ﷺ) died, and he said: 'Wash her an odd number of times, three, or five, or more than that if you see fit, and wash her with water and sidr (lote-tree leaves), and put camphor, or something of camphor, in the last (washing), and when you have finished, inform me.' So when we finished, we informed him, and he threw us his waist-wrapper and said: 'Shroud her in it (as the innermost garment next to her body).'""

Hushaim said: ""And in the narration of others - not these narrators - and I do not know, perhaps Hisham was among them - she said: 'And we plaited her hair into three braids.'"" Hushaim said: ""I think he said: 'And we laid it behind her.'""

Hushaim said: ""Khalid, from among the group, narrated to us from Hafsah and Muhammad, from Umm 'Atiyyah, who said: 'And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: ""Begin with her right side and the places of wudu.""'""

There is also a narration on this topic from Umm Sulaim.

Abu 'Eisa said: The hadith of Umm 'Atiyyah is a hasan sahih hadith. This is what is acted upon according to the people of knowledge. It has been narrated from Ibrahim An-Nakha'i that he said: ""The washing of the deceased is like the washing for major ritual impurity (janabah)."" Malik bin Anas said: ""There is no fixed limit for washing the deceased according to us, and there is no known specific description for it, rather it is (simply) that he be purified."" Ash-Shafi'i said: ""Malik only said a general statement: 'He is washed and cleaned.' If the deceased is cleaned with plain water or other water, that suffices for his washing, but it is more beloved to me that he be washed three times or more, not less than three, because of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Wash her three times or five.' And if they are cleaned in less than three times, that suffices, and it is not held that the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ) means anything other than achieving cleanliness with three or five, and he did not specify a fixed limit."" The jurists have said likewise, and they are more knowledgeable about the meanings of the hadith. Ahmad and Ishaq said: ""The washings should be with water and sidr, and in the last one there should be something of camphor."""
"993","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Ghusl for one who washed him and Wudu for one who carried himm"
"994","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Wear the white among your garments"
"995","Abu Qatadah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When one of you shrouds his brother"
"996","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Wear the white among your garments, for indeed they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them."""
"997","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah shrouded Hamzah bin Abdul-Muttalib in one cloth of Namirah"
"998","Aishah said: ""The Prophet was shrouded in three white Yemeni cloths, there was no shirt nor turban among them."" He said: ""So they mentioned the saying of the others to Aishah, that there were two garments and a Habir Burd. She said: 'A Burd was brought, but they refused it and they did not shroud him in it.'"""
"999","Abdullah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""He who slaps (his) cheeks"
"1000","""When the news of the death of Ja'far came, the Prophet said: 'Prepare some food for the family of Ja'far, for indeed something has happened to them that will keep them busy.'"""
"1001","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""There are four matters in my nation that are from the matters of Jahiliyyah which the people will not leave: Wailing"
"1002","""A man died among the Ansar named Qarazah bin Ka'b, and he was being wailed over. So Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah came and ascended the Minbar. He uttered thanks and praise to Allah and said: ""As for the gravity of wailing in Islam, indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: 'The one who is wailed over is punished as long as he is being wailed over.'"""
"1003","Musa bin Abi Musa Al-Asha'ri narrated from his father that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""No one dies and they stand over him crying and saying: 'O what a great man he was! O how respectful he was!' except that two angels are appointed for him to poke him (saying): 'Is that you?"
"1004","Yahya bin Abdur-Rahman narrated from Ibn Umar that:The Prophet said: ""The deceased is punished for the crying of his family over him."" So"
"1005","The Messenger of Allah said: ""No one dies and they stand over him crying and saying: 'O what a great man he was! O how respectful he was!' except that two angels are appointed for him to poke him (saying): 'Is that you?'"""
"1006","The Prophet said: ""The deceased is punished for the crying of his family over him."" So, Aishah said: ""May Allah have mercy upon him. He has not lied, but he is mistaken. It is only that the Messenger of Allah said about a Jewish man who died: 'The deceased is being punished and his family is crying over him.'"""
"1007","# Hadith Translation

**Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrated:**

The Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) took the hand of 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Awf (may Allāh be pleased with him) and went with him to his son Ibrāhīm, whom he found in his final agony. The Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) took the child, placed him in his lap, and wept. 'Abd al-Raḥmān said, ""Do you weep? Did you not forbid weeping?"" He (ṣallallahu 'alayhi wa sallam) replied, **""No, but I forbade two foolish and sinful sounds: wailing at a beating of faces, tearing of garments, and the voice of Shayṭān.""**

There is additional wording in the narration.

**Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** *This is a ḥasan (good) hadith.*

---

*Note: This narration is recorded by al-Tirmidhī, who graded it ḥasan. It demonstrates the permissibility of silent tears (al-bukā') out of compassion and natural human grief, while prohibiting excessive lamentation and self-harm associated with pre-Islamic practices of mourning.*"
"1008","Amrah informed him that she heard Aishah, while it was being mentioned to her that Ibn Umar had said that the deceased would be punished for the crying of the living (over him). So Aishah said: 'May Allah forgive Abu Abdur-Rahman. He has not lied, but he is mistaken in the understanding. Rather, the Messenger of Allah passed by a Jewish woman who was being cried over, so he said: 'They are crying over her and she is being punished in her grave.'"""
"1009","Narrated Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, Ahmad ibn Mani', Ishaq ibn Mansur, and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, who said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said:

""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking ahead of the funeral procession."""
"1010","Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Messenger of Allah would walk in front of the funeral"
"1011","# Hadith of Ibn 'Umar: Walking Before the Janazah

**Narrated by Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them):**

'Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us — 'Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us — Ma'mar informed us — from az-Zuhri, who said:

The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to walk **before** the janazah (funeral procession).

Az-Zuhri said: And Salim informed me that his father ['Umar ibn al-Khattab] used to walk before the janazah.

He [at-Tirmidhi] said: And in this chapter there is also a narration from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him).

**Abu 'Isa (at-Tirmidhi) said:** The hadith of Ibn 'Umar in this manner was narrated by Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad ibn Sa'd, and others besides them, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, similar to the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah.

And Ma'mar, Yunus ibn Yazid, Malik, and other huffāth (preservers of hadith) narrated from az-Zuhri that the Prophet ﷺ used to walk before the janazah. Az-Zuhri said: And Salim informed me that his father used to walk before the janazah.

The people of hadith are unanimous in their view that the **mursal** (disconnected) hadith on this matter is the more authentic one.

**Abu 'Isa said:** I heard Yahya ibn Musa saying that 'Abd ar-Razzaq said that Ibn al-Mubarak said: ""The hadith of az-Zuhri on this matter is mursal, and it is more authentic than the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah.""

Ibn al-Mubarak further said: ""And I believe that Ibn Jurayj took it from Ibn 'Uyaynah.""

**Abu 'Isa said:** And Hammam ibn Yahya narrated this hadith from Ziyad — who is ibn Sa'd — and Mansur, Bakr, and Sufyan, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father. However, the Sufyan in this chain is actually **Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah**, from whom Hammam narrated it.

**The Difference of Opinion Among the Scholars Regarding Walking Before the Janazah:**

The scholars have differed concerning walking before the janazah. Some of the scholars from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others held the view that walking **before** it is **more virtuous** (afdal). This is the position of **Imam ash-Shafi'i** and **Imam Ahmad** (may Allah have mercy on them both).

He [at-Tirmidhi] said: And the hadith of Anas in this chapter is **not preserved** (ghayr mahfuz)."
"1012","Thawban narrated:""We went with the Prophet (following) a funeral. He saw people riding so he said: 'Are you not ashamed? Indeed Allah's angels are on their feet"
"1013","From Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: ""We asked the Messenger of Allah about walking behind the funeral. He said: 'Less than a trot. For if he was good, then you will be hastening him to it (goodness), and if he was evil, then it id only an inhabitant of the Fire that is being taken away.""  The funeral is (to be) followed. The one who precedes it shall not have the reward of those who follow it.'"""
"1014","""We went with the Prophet (following) a funeral. He saw people riding so he said: 'Are you not ashamed? Indeed Allah's angels are on their feet, while you are on the backs of your beasts'"""
"1015","""We were with the Prophet (following) the funeral of Ibn Ad-Dahbah, and he was on a horse that was walking quickly, and we were around him, and he was trotting."""
"1016","Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Messenger of Allah came to Hamza on the Day of Uhud"
"1017","The Prophet said: ""Hurry up with the funeral (procession) for if it was good, you are advancing it to good, and if it was evil, then you are taking it off your necks."""
"1018","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us; Abū Ṣafwān narrated to us, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihāb, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:**

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon Ḥamzah on the day of Uḥud and stood over him. He saw that his body had been mutilated. He ﷺ said: **""Were it not that Ṣafiyyah would be grieved, I would have left him until the wild beasts devoured him, so that he would be resurrected on the Day of Judgment from their bellies.""**

He ﷺ then called for a *namirah* (a worn-out cloak) and shrouded him in it. However, when it was spread over his head, his legs became exposed, and when it was spread over his legs, his head became exposed.

He said: **The number of martyrs had grown great, and the garments had become scarce.** Thus, one man, two men, and even three men were shrouded in a single garment and buried together in one grave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask about them: **""Which of them had memorized the most Qurʾān?""** and would advance that one toward the *qiblah*.

He said: **The Messenger of Allah ﷺ buried them and did not offer the funeral prayer over them.**

Abū ʿĪsā said: **The Ḥadīth of Anas is a *ḥasan gharīb* (good and singular) Ḥadīth. We do not know it from the Ḥadīth of Anas except through this chain.**

**The *namirah* is a worn-out garment.**

Usāmad ibn Zayd was contradicted in the narration of this Ḥadīth. **Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh.** And **Maʿmar narrated it from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Thaʿlabah, from Jābir.**

We do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhrī on the authority of Anas except Usāmah ibn Zayd.

**I asked Muḥammad (al-Bukhārī) about this Ḥadīth, and he said: ""The Ḥadīth of Layth, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from Jābir, is more authentic.""**

---

*Ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam.*"
"1019","""The Messenger of Allah would visit the sick, attend the funerals, ride a donkey, accept the invitation of a slave, and on the Day of Banu Quraizah he was on a donkey muzzled with a cord of fibers and a pack-saddle made of fibers."""
"1020","""When the Messenger of Allah died, they disagreed over where to bury him. So Abu Bakr said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah saying something which I have not forgotten, he said: ""Allah does not take (the life of ) a Prophet except at the location in which He wants him to be buried.'"" So they buried him at the spot of his bed."""
"1021","Abu Sinan said:""I buried my son Sinan and Abu Talhah Al-Khawlani was sitting on the rim of the grave. When I wanted to leave he took me by my hand and said: 'Shall I not inform you of some good new O Abu Sinan!' I said: 'Of course.' He said: 'Ad-Dahhak bin Abdur-Rahman bin Arzab narrated to me"
"1022","""When the Messenger of Allah follows a corpse, he would not sit until (the deceased was) placed in the Lahd. A rabbi came upon him and said: 'This is what we do, O Muhammad'"" He said: ""So the Messenger of Allah sat, and he said: 'Differ from them.'"""
"1023","""I buried my son Sinan and Abu Talhah Al-Khawlani was sitting on the rim of the grave. When I wanted to leave he took me by my hand and said: 'Shall I not inform you of some good new O Abu Sinan!' I said: 'Of course.' He said: 'Ad-Dahhak bin Abdur-Rahman bin Arzab narrated to me, from Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari: ""The Messenger of Allah said: 'When a child of the slave (of Allah) died, Allah says to the angels: ""Have you taken the fruits of his work."" They reply: ""Yes."" So He says: ""What did My slave say?"" They reply: ""He praised you and mentioned that to You is the return."" So Allah says: ""Build a house in Paradise for My slave, and name it 'the house of praise.'"""
"1024","Abu Ibrahim Al-Ashhali narrated :from his father who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah would perform the Salat for the funeral he would said: (Allahammaghfir li-hayyina wa mayyittina"
"1025","# Hadith Translation

**Narrated by Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him):**

Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said:

""Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pronounce the takbīr (i.e., say *Allāhu Akbar*) over our funeral prayers four times. Then he pronounced the takbīr over a funeral five times, so we asked him about that. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pronounce it (five times).'""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""The ḥadīth of Zayd ibn Arqam is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ (good and authentic) ḥadīth.""

He further stated: ""Some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and others held this view, considering the takbīr over the funeral prayer to be five.""

He added: ""Aḥmad (ibn Ḥanbal) and Isḥāq (ibn Rāhawayh) said: 'If the imām pronounces five takbīrs over the funeral, then the imām is to be followed (i.e., the congregation should follow the imām in this).'""

---

**Source:** *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī* — Chapter on Funeral Prayers (Kitāb al-Janāʾiz)"
"1026","from his father who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah would perform  the Salat for the funeral he would said: (Allahammaghfir li-hayyina wa mayyittina, wa shahidina wa gha'ibina, wa saghirina wa kabirina, wa dhakarina wa unthana) 'O Allah! Forgive our living and our deceased, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female.'"""
"1027","""I heard the Messenger of Allah, while he was performing Salat for a deceased person. I could hear him saying in his prayer: (Allahummagfir lahu, war hamhu, waghsilhu bil-baradi (waghsilhu) kama yughsaluth-thawb) 'O Allah! Forgive him, have mercy upon him, and wash him with (snow or ice) (and wash him) just as a garment is washed.'"""
"1028","Marthan bin Abdullah Al-Yazani narrated:""When Malik bin Hubairah performed Salat for a funeral and the people were few he would divide them into three groups (rows) then say: 'The Messenger of Allah said: ""For whomever three rows perform Salat"
"1029","""Ibn Abbas performed Salat for a funeral and he recited Fatihatil-Kitab. So I asked him about it and he said: 'It is from the Sunnah' or, 'From the completeness of the Sunnah.'"""
"1030","""When Malik bin Hubairah performed Salat for a funeral and the people were few he would divide them into three groups (rows) then say: 'The Messenger of Allah said: ""For whomever three rows perform Salat, then it is granted."""
"1031","The Prophet said: ""No one among the Muslim dies, and Salat is performed for him by a community of Muslims reaching one hundred, and they intercede (supplicate) for him, except that their intercession for him is accepted."" In his narration, 'Ali bin Hujr said: ""One hundred or more than that."""
"1032","""There are three times that the Messenger of Allah prohibited us from performing Salat in, burying our dead in: When the sun's rising appears until it has risen up; when the sun is at the zenith until it passes, and when the sun begins its setting, until it has set."""
"1033","The Prophet said: ""The rider is to be behind the funeral (procession), and the walker where he wishes, and the child should be prayed over."""
"1034","The Prophet said: ""The child is not prayed over, nor does he inherit, nor is he inherited from until one is sure he was alive at birth."""
"1035","Samurah bin Jundab narrated:""The Prophet prayed over a woman, so he stood at her middle."""
"1036","""I prayed for the funeral of a man with Anas bin Malik, so he stood parallel to his head. Then they came with the body of a woman from the Quraish. They said: 'O Abu Hamzah perform the prayer for her.' So he stood parallel to her waist. Al-Ala bin Ziyad said to him: 'Is this how you saw the Messenger of Allah standing in the place for the funeral as you did for her, and for a place that you stood for the man?' He said: 'Yes.' When he was finished he said: 'Remember (this).'"""
"1037","Ash-Shaibani narrated that:Ash-Sha'bi said: ""I was informed by one who saw the Prophet: He (pbuh) saw a solitary grave"
"1038","Jabir bin Abdullah informed him that the Prophet had put two men together in one cloth from those who were killed at (the battle of) Uhud, then he said: ""Which of them memorized the more of the Qur'an?"" When one of them was indicated to him, he put him in the Lahd (first) and said: ""I am a witness for those people on the Day of Judgment."" And he ordered that they be buried in their blood, and that they not be prayed over, nor washed."
"1039","Imran bin Husain narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Indeed your brother An-Najashi has died. So stand to perform Salat for him."" He (Imran) said: ""We stood and lined up just as the deceased is lined up for"
"1040","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever performs the funeral prayer then he will get a reward equal to a Qirat. Whoever follows it until it is buried then he will get a reward equal to two Qirat"
"1041","Narrated by Abu Salamah, Yahya ibn Khalaf, and Humayd ibn Mas'adah, who both said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Muhallab, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, who said:

The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to us: ""Indeed, your brother the Negus has died, so stand and pray over him."" He said: So we stood and lined up as one lines up for the deceased, and we prayed over him as one prays over the deceased.

In this chapter, there are narrations from Abu Hurayrah, Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, Abu Sa'id, Hudhayfah ibn Asid, and Jarir ibn 'Abdullah.

Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih gharib hadith from this chain. Abu Qilabah narrated it from his uncle, Abu al-Muhallab, from 'Imran ibn Husayn. Abu al-Muhallab's name is 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr, and it is also said Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr."
"1042","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever performs the funeral prayer then he will get a reward equal to a Qirat. Whoever follows it until it is buried then he will get a reward equal to two Qirat, one of them, or the least of them, is similar to Uhud (mountain)."" This was mentioned to Ibn Umar, so he sent a message to Aishah to ask her about that, and she said: ""Abu Hurairah has told the truth."" So Ibn Umar said: ""We have missed many Qirat."""
"1043","""I accompanied Abu Hurairah for ten years, and I heard him saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Whoever follows a funeral, and carries it three times, then he has fulfilled the right that is required from him."""
"1044","Mas'ud bin Al-Hakim narrated that standing for the funeral (procession) until it is put down was mentioned"
"1045","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whenever you see a funeral (procession), stand up (for it). Whoever follows it, then do not sit down until it is put down."""
"1046","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood, then (later) he sat"". (Sahih)


There are narrations on this topic from Al-Hasan bin 'Ali, and Ibn 'Abbas. 


Abu Eisa said: The Hadith of 'Ali is a Hasan Sahih Hadith, regarding which there are narrations from four of the Tabi'in narrating it from each other. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. Ash-Shafi'i said: ""This is the most correct thing on this topic"" This Hadith abrogates first Hadith: ""Whenever you see a funeral (procession), stand up .""


Ahmad said: ""If he wants, he stands, and if he wants, he does not stand."" His proof is that it has been reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) stood, then sat, and this is what Ishaq bin Ibrahim said.


(Abu Eisa said:) As for the saying of 'Ali: The Prophet (ﷺ) stood for the funeral and then sat, he means that the Prophet (ﷺ) would stand when he saw a funeral (procession), then he did not do so later, so he would not stand when he saw the funeral (procession)."
"1047","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated that:His father said: ""The one who made the Lahd in the grave of the Messenger of Allah was Abu Talhah. And the one who placed the velvet cloth under him was Shuqran a freed slave of Messenger of Allah"
"1048","""When he Prophet put the deceased in the grave"" He said: And Abu Khalid (one of the narrators) said : ""When he placed the deceased in the Lahd"" - ""He said one time: 'In the Name of Allah, by His command and upon the Millah of the Messenger of Allah.' and one time he said: 'In the Name of Allah, by His command and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."""
"1049","Abu Wa'il narrated:""Ali said to Abu Al-Hayyaj Al-Asadi: 'I am dispatching you with what the Prophet dispatched me: ""That you not leave an elevated grave without leveling it"
"1050","Abu Marthan Al-Ghanawi narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Do not sit on the graves nor perform Salat towards them"
"1051","""Ali said to Abu Al-Hayyaj Al-Asadi: 'I am dispatching you with what the Prophet dispatched me: ""That you not leave an elevated grave without leveling it, nor an image without erasing it."""
"1052","Jabir narrated:""The Messenger of Allah prohibited plastering graves"
"1053","from the Prophet, similar (to no. 1050), but it does not contain ""From Abu Idris"" and this is what is correct."
"1054","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated from his father that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""I had prohibited you from visiting the graves. But Muhammad was permitted to visit the grave of his mother: so visit them"
"1055","Abdullah bin Abi Mulaikah said:""Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr died in Al-Hubshi"" He said: ""He was carried to Makkah to be buried there. So when Aishah arrived she went to the grave of Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr and she said: ""We were like two drinking companions of Jadhimah for such a long time that they would say: 'They will never part.' So when we were separated it was as if I and Malik - due to the length of unity - never spent a night together"
"1056","The Messenger of Allah said: ""I had prohibited you from visiting the graves. But Muhammad was permitted to visit the grave of his mother: so visit them, for they will remind you of the Hereafter."""
"1057","""Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr died in Al-Hubshi"" He said: ""He was carried to Makkah to be buried there. So when Aishah arrived she went to the grave of Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr and she said: ""We were like two drinking companions of Jadhimah for such a long time that they would say: 'They will never part.' So when we were separated it was as if I and Malik - due to the length of unity - never spent a night together."""
"1058","Anas bin Malik narrated:""A funeral (procession) passed by the Messenger of Allah and they were praising him with good statements. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Granted.' Then he said: 'You are Allah's witnesses on the earth"
"1059","""The Prophet entered a grave during the night, so a torch was lit for him. He took it (the deceased) in from the direction of the Qiblah, and he said: 'May Allah have mercy upon you, you were often invoking (Allah) by reciting the Qur'an.' And he said: 'Allahu Akbar four times."""
"1060","""A funeral (procession) passed by the Messenger of Allah and they were praising him with good statements. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Granted.' Then he said: 'You are Allah's witnesses on the earth.'"""
"1061","""I arrived in Al-Madinah and while I was sitting with Umar bin Al-Khattab they passed by with a funeral, over (a person) whom they were praising with good. Umar said: 'Granted.' I said to Umar: 'What is granted?' He said: 'I said as the Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no Muslim about whom three bear witness, except that he is granted Paradise."" He said: ""And two (as well)."" He said: 'We did not ask the Messenger of Allah about one.'"""
"1062","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, from Mālik ibn Anas, and al-Anṣārī narrated to us, Ma'n narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:**

*""No Muslim shall have three of his children die without the Fire touching them, except for the fulfilment of the oath.""*

He (the compiler) said: **""In this chapter, there are narrations from 'Umar, Mu'ād, Ka'b ibn Mālik, 'Utbah ibn 'Abd, Umm Sulaym, Jābir, Anas, Abū Dharr, Ibn Mas'ūd, Abū Tha'labah al-Ashja'ī, Ibn 'Abbās, 'Uqbah ibn 'Āmir, Abū Sa'īd, and Qurrah ibn Iyās al-Muzanī.""**

He said: **""And Abū Tha'labah al-Ashja'ī has only one hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and it is this hadith, and he is not al-Khushanī.""**

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""The hadith of Abū Hurayrah is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* (good and authentic) hadith.""**

---

### Notes on Key Terms:

- **"""
"1063","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever has three that precede him (in death) while they did not reach the age of puberty, then they will be a well-fortified fortress for him against the Fire."""
"1064","""I heard my grandfather, the father of my mother, Simak bin Al-Walid Al-Hanadi narrating, that he heard Ibn Abbas narrated, that he heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Whoever has two predecessors (in death) among my Ummah, then Allah will admit them into Paradise.""So Aishah said to him: ""What about one from your Ummar who has one precessor?"" He (pbuh) said: ""And whoever has one predecessor O Muwaffaqqah!"" So she said: ""What about one who does not have a predecessor from your Ummah?"" He said: ""I am the predecessor for my Ummah: you will never suffer (in grief) for (the loss of) anyone similar to me."""
"1065","Usamah bin Zaid narrated that:The Prophet mentioned the plague and said: ""It is an abiding punishment or chastisement that was sent upon a group of the children of Isra'il. So when it occurs in a land while you are in it"
"1066","""Sulaiman bin Surad said to Khalid bin Urfutah - or, Khalid said to Sulaiman - 'Did you hear the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Whoever is killed by his stomach then he will not be punished in the grave""?' One of them said to the other: ""Yes."""
"1067","The Prophet mentioned the plague and said: ""It is an abiding punishment or chastisement that was sent upon a group of the children of Isra'il. So when it occurs in a land while you are in it, then do not leave it. And when it occurs in a land while you are not in it, then do not enter it."""
"1068","Narrated by 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him.""

This hadith is also narrated through chains of transmission from Abu Musa, Abu Hurairah, and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with them all).

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit is a hasan sahih (good and authentic) hadith."
"1069","Aishah mentioned that the Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, then Allah loves to meet him. And whoever dislikes meeting Allah, then Allah dislikes meeting him."" She said: ""O Messenger of Allah! All of us dislike death."" He said: ""It is not like that. But when the believer is given the good news of Allah's mercy, His pleasure, and His Paradise, then he loves to meet Allah and Allah loves to meet him. Whereas when the disbeliever is given the news of Allah's punishment and His wrath, he dislikes meeting Allah, and Allah dislikes meeting him."""
"1070","Abu Hurairah narrated:""A deceased man would be brought to the Messenger of Allah while a debt was due upon him. So he would say: 'Has he left anything to pay off his debt?' If he was told that he had left something to pay it then he would pray (the funeral prayer) for him. Otherwise he would tell the Muslims: 'Pray for your companion.' So when Allah granted him the victories"
"1071","The Prophet was brought a (deceased) man to perform Salat over. So the Prophet said: ""Pray for your companion; for indeed he had a debt upon him."" Abu Qatadah said: ""It shall be upon me."" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""To pay it off?"" (He said: ""To pay it off."") So he performed the prayer for him."
"1072","""A deceased man would be brought to the Messenger of Allah while a debt was due upon him. So he would say: 'Has he left anything to pay off his debt?' If he was told that he had left something to pay it then he would pray (the funeral prayer) for him. Otherwise he would tell the Muslims: 'Pray for your companion.' So when Allah granted him the victories, he stood and said: 'I am more worthy in the case of the believers than they themselves are. So whoever among the believers dies and leaves a debt behind, then it is up to me to fulfill it. And whoever leaves wealth behind, then it is for his heirs.'"""
"1073","The Messenger of Allah said: ""When the deceased - or he said when one of you - is buried, two angels, black and blue (eyed_ come to him. One of them is called Al-Munkar, and the other An-Nakir. They say: 'What did you used to say about this man?' So he says what he was saying (before death) 'He is Allah's slave and His Messenger. I testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah and that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger.' So they say: 'We knew that you would say this.' Then his grave is expanded to seventy by seventy cubits, then it is illuminated for him. Then it is said to him: 'Sleep.' So he said: 'Can I return to my family to inform them?' They say: 'Sleep as a newlywed, whom none awakens but the dearest of his family.' Until Allah resurrects him from his resting place.""""If he was a hypocrite he would say: 'I heard people saying something, so I said the same; I do not know.' So they said: 'We knew you would say that.' So the earth is told: 'Constrict him.' So it constricts around him, squeezing his ribs together. He continues being punished like that until Allah resurrects him from his resting place."""
"1074","The Messenger of Allah said: ""When a person dies, he is shown his place . If he is one of the people of Paradise; he is shown his place among the people of Paradise, and if he one of the people of the Fire; he is shown his place among the people of the Fire. Then it is said to him: 'This is your place until Allah resurrects you on the Day of Judgment.'"""
"1075","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said to him: ""O Ali! Three are not to be delayed: Salat when it is due"
"1076","The Messenger of Allah said: ""No Muslim dies on the day of Friday, nor the night of Friday, except that Allah protects him from the trials of the grave."""
"1077","It is narrated from Qutaybah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Juhanī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, from his father, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"
"1078","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The believer's soul is suspended by his debt until it is settled for him"
"1079","(Another chain) Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The believer's soul is suspended by his debt until it is settled for him"
